INDUCTORS
This are device design to take advantage of the effect of electromagnetic induction/cause. Circular radiating magnetic field can be generated when a current flows through wire anytime, increasing or decreasing a current flow will relatively increase or decrease the magnetic field strength.  Just like capacitor that stores voltage or electric energy in the form of electric field, electric field can also be stored in a magnetic field. Theoretically, any device capable od generating a magnetic field has inductance. A device that has inductance is referred to as an inductor.
Electromagnetism
According to the law of electromagnetism, the field of a charge at rest can be represented by a uniform, radial distribution of electric field lines or lines of force.  For a moving charge at a constant velocity, the field lines are still radial and straight but they are no longer uniformly distributed. At the same time, the electron generates a circular magnetic field. If the charge accelerates, things get a bit more complex and a ‘kink’ is created in the electromagnetic field, giving rise to an electromagnetic wave that radiates outs.

The simple way to generate a magnetic field is to pass a current through a conductor. Inductors are device used to resist change in current. Symbol for inductor is -mmm—(not exactly like this).  It is measured in Henry , H. When the applied voltage increases, it acts like a time-dependent resistor whose resistance is greatest during time of rapid increase in current. On the other hand, when the applied voltage decreases, the inductor act like a time- dependent voltage source attempting to keep current flowing.
    Inductors also stores energy just like capacitor but in it magnetic field and later returns it to the circuit when the magnetic field collapses.
